{"id":"I01","text":"Hi! Let's count Fibonacci numbers, and watch each new number take shape.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I01.wav","duration_s":4.213541666666667,"sha256":"20f686194e94c4ba892f69e4e58aa0a14fa76201283a1ccff46e845e9f505742","trim":{"raw_duration_s":4.95,"leading_s":0.28858333333333336,"trailing_s":0.447875,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I02","text":"We start with zero and one. These are our two starting values.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I02.wav","duration_s":3.5311666666666666,"sha256":"28dee23c66e8490be373b12dee16a0d4cf756cc3367b7b49120a2f1c6b18b1b6","trim":{"raw_duration_s":4.275,"leading_s":0.31566666666666665,"trailing_s":0.42816666666666664,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I03","text":"To make the next number, add the previous two. Then use the newest pair, and do it again.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I03.wav","duration_s":4.9155,"sha256":"8f7bb5ae539a7c6ac3dd4aba711c81a92f3110e8e14634b9c3ca652cb003fc51","trim":{"raw_duration_s":5.65,"leading_s":0.28008333333333335,"trailing_s":0.4544166666666667,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I04","text":"The small labels tell us each number's place. We start at F zero, so F two is the third entry.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I04.wav","duration_s":6.0852916666666665,"sha256":"505c494fb5c0df00e82fb1beb80599afd42ca7be0983fdebd7277723b14428da","trim":{"raw_duration_s":6.875,"leading_s":0.30525,"trailing_s":0.4844583333333333,"peak_normalization_gain":0.9664306064868738},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I05","text":"The older value sits on the left. The newer value sits beside it. Their labels move with them.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I05.wav","duration_s":5.413541666666666,"sha256":"92c305138135ae19fc82b76dbcbaf0acef390768e56b0468f2ff4c3ecf956e5c","trim":{"raw_duration_s":6.2,"leading_s":0.318875,"trailing_s":0.46758333333333335,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I06","text":"Listen for plus and equals. The answer appears when we say its name, and becomes our newest value.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I06.wav","duration_s":5.929916666666666,"sha256":"a7773cb89f06c3fde6775e7d2e0d5c8ee7722d752d45b059a5329e435dda297e","trim":{"raw_duration_s":6.7,"leading_s":0.2966666666666667,"trailing_s":0.47341666666666665,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I07","text":"Number windows show values, not piles of things. A window marked one thousand stands for that value, not one thousand objects.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I07.wav","duration_s":7.973416666666667,"sha256":"b74cf59846384eceb6fbdd98d0c570e7857597bb34ab402a603d6868734f987a","trim":{"raw_duration_s":8.725,"leading_s":0.3124166666666667,"trailing_s":0.43916666666666665,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I08","text":"We'll keep adding until the sequence first passes one hundred million. The numbers grow, but the rule stays the same.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I08.wav","duration_s":6.700666666666667,"sha256":"8a89afcbdced59de06ddba0bcdcb1c1d3e714d3a6ef7fe1414cc18ba70f1ac8e","trim":{"raw_duration_s":7.45,"leading_s":0.289625,"trailing_s":0.45970833333333333,"peak_normalization_gain":0.961578591060009},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
