{"id":"T008a","text":"Let's look inside that addition. In the ones column, eight plus three makes eleven: one stays here, and one ten moves left.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/T008a.wav","duration_s":7.560125,"sha256":"41ea6bb5409b09c5fba7411b93b4a27fe5599f66bd148137846485a2d4c2adb2","trim":{"raw_duration_s":8.3,"leading_s":0.298,"trailing_s":0.441875,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"T008b","text":"That carried ten joins the ten already there. The columns now show two tens and one one. Then the newest pair moves on.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/fibonacci-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/T008b.wav","duration_s":7.438916666666667,"sha256":"2b60a03986a86747fcb6854f1f113382241ef685ee550d6861caf60946743a38","trim":{"raw_duration_s":8.225,"leading_s":0.31275,"trailing_s":0.47333333333333333,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
